-- title:
--   Joint injectivity of points of the localised Hecke algebra T_{θ'}
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field $k=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$, i.e. a $2$-dimensional $k$-vector space $\bar\rho.V$ with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(\bar\rho.V)$ trivial on the subgroup fixing some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, assumed absolutely irreducible (its base change to an algebraic closure of $k$ has no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$). Let $S\supseteq S_0$ be finite sets of naturals with every element of $S$ prime and $p\in S$, and let $N\neq 0$ be such that every prime factor of $N$ lies in $S$ and outside $S_0$, with $p^2\nmid N$; assume $\bar\rho$ is unramified at each $q\in S$ with $q\neq p$, $q\nmid N$ (trivial on the inertia subgroups of all valuation subrings of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit); for each prime $q\neq p$ with $q\mid N$, $q^2\nmid N$, that $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$ and that inertia at $q$ acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; for each prime $q\neq p$ with $q^2\mid N$, that $q^3\nmid N$ and inertia at $q$ again acts with characteristic polynomial $(X-1)^2$; and, if $p\mid N$, that $\bar\rho$ is ordinary at $p$, i.e. over every valuation subring above $p$ there is a line spanned by a basis vector, stable under the decomposition group, containing $(\bar\rho(\sigma)-1)v$ for all inertia elements $\sigma$ and all $v$. Assume weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are integers. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$) and $U_q$ ($q$ prime, $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$), and assume: for $\ell\neq p$ prime, $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S_0$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\ell$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ which is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$ (lying in the decomposition group and acting as $x\mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field) satisfy $\mathrm{charpoly}(\bar\rho(\sigma))=X^2-\theta'(T_\ell)X+\ell$; $\theta'(U_q)=0$ whenever $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$ and $q^2\mid N$; $\theta'(U_q)$ equals the trace of any endomorphism of the inertia coinvariants $\bar\rho.V/\sum_{\tau\in I_P}\mathrm{im}(\bar\rho(\tau)-1)$ induced by a Frobenius $\sigma$ at $q$, whenever $q\mid N$, $q\notin S_0$, $q^2\nmid N$; and likewise $\theta'(T_p)$ equals the trace of any endomorphism of the inertia coinvariants at $p$ induced by a Frobenius at $p$, when $p\nmid N$ and $p\notin S_0$. Then there are a natural number $n$ and a family $A_0,\dots,A_{n-1}$ of complete discrete valuation rings, each a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, each an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra which is module-finite over $\mathcal{O}$ with local structure map, together with $\mathcal{O}$-algebra homomorphisms $\chi_i$ from the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S₀ 𝒪 θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) of the $\mathcal{O}$-base-changed Hecke lattice at the prime cut out by $\theta'$ to $A_i$, such that each $\chi_i$ is a local homomorphism and the $\chi_i$ are jointly injective: an element annihilated by all of them is zero.
--
--   This is the statement that an identity in the localised full weight-two Hecke algebra $\mathbb{T}_{\theta'}$ of level $N$ away from $S_0$ may be tested on its points valued in complete discrete valuation rings finite over $\mathcal{O}$, the analogue for the full algebra of the corresponding result for the anemic one. It is obtained from the reducedness statement [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.isReduced_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.isReduced_of_charpoly_frobenius_eq_of_isAbsolutelyIrreducible), which carries the arithmetic content, and is used in the identification of Hecke eigenvalues with $q$-expansion coefficients and with unit roots at $p$.
